1
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:09,040
YAMU, YAMU, YAMU, YAMU!

2
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:31,498
You're on the move!

3
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:09,140
Thanks to the seal of Orikakos,
I've just sealed the duel, Kaiba.

4
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:11,760
Soon you'll be losing your soul,

5
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,157
but it wouldn't be the first
time that happened to you, right?

6
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:16,070
That's enough.

7
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:17,780
No more tricks, Alistair.

8
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:19,390
Seto!

9
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:22,290
Mokuba!

10
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:24,660
Did that seem like a trick to you?

11
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:26,860
Let my brother out!

12
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,997
Who do you think you are, anyway?

13
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:34,837
You have no idea who you're messing
with sure I do I'm messing with a greedy

14
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:39,800
little punk who's just as pathetic as
his old man What did you just say to me?

15
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:43,577
No one compares me to my
stepfather and gets away with it.

16
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:45,013
Do I make myself clear?

17
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:48,160
He was a worthless snake like you

18
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:53,497
My family business has nothing
to do with you guess again

19
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:58,120
your family business has everything
to do with me All right, Alistair.

20
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,680
Who put you up to this?

21
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,200
No one did.

22
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:05,457
I'm here to represent every single person

23
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:08,128
whose life was ripped
apart by your company.

24
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:09,635
And more importantly,

25
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:15,200
I'm here to make sure you're never able
to step on anyone ever again. Get in line.

26
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:17,580
I hear that speech every day.

27
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:23,860
Punch buggy green. No backsies. Ow!

28
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:25,917
There's not a car around for miles.

29
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,440
Oops, my bad.

30
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:30,360
Hey, you all right, Yug?

31
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:33,493
Well, I've been better.

32
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:34,600
How about you?

33
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:36,434
Well, I've been worse.

34
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:41,257
Aren't you guys worried about what
Pegasus said on that videotape yesterday?

35
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:42,752
Someone's following him.

36
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:46,117
And I have a feeling it's
the same biker gang that

37
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:49,057
stole the Egyptian god cars
from my grandpa's shop.

38
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:49,970
Me too.

39
00:02:50,053 --> 00:02:52,940
If they found him, we could
be walking into a trap.

40
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:55,157
Let's get on with this.

41
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:57,920
I summon Gorlag in attack mode.

42
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:04,220
And here's a little bonus.

43
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:09,800
Your monster just got stronger. But how?

44
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:12,360
Remember the Seal of Orichalcos?

45
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:14,877
As long as it stays active on the field,

46
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:18,700
every one of my monsters gets
a 500 attack point boost. What?

47
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:19,800
You heard me.

48
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:25,320
Plus my Gorlag gets another 500 points
for every fire monster on the field.

49
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:27,700
There are none. Oh, no?

50
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:31,300
What do you think my Gorlag's made of?

51
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:36,740
Ready, Gorlag?

52
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:40,440
Attack his Versago the Destroyer, now!

53
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:49,000
What's that?

54
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:52,712
Did I forget to mention my
Gorlag's other special ability?

55
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:56,097
Every time he destroys one
of my opponent's monsters,

56
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:59,960
that very same monster reappears
on my side of the field.

57
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:03,360
Only this time, it becomes
a creature of fire!

58
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:14,249
And you remember what happens when a
creature of fire is on the field, right?

59
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:16,320
My Gorlack gets even stronger!

60
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:19,180
It's over for you!

61
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:22,540
No way!

62
00:04:22,740 --> 00:04:25,620
Every monster Seto loses
becomes Alistair's.

63
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:27,878
His old deck could turn against him.

64
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:34,000
Now that I've placed one card
face down, I'll end my turn.

65
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:36,920
This wacko has more skill than I thought.

66
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:39,000
But too bad for him.

67
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:40,080
I'm better.

68
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:43,420
And I've got just the
cards to take him down.

69
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:47,917
Once my virus combination
infects his gore lag,

70
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,660
Every monster he stole
from me will be gone.

71
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:53,340
Then his life points will be wide open.

72
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,720
It's showtime, so stand back.

73
00:04:58,440 --> 00:05:01,800
First, I summon Pitch Dark
Dragon in defense mode.

74
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:07,200
Then I place this face down.

75
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:10,614
Let me guess, that's Crush Card, right?

76
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:14,100
I've had my eye on you
for a long time, Kaiba,

77
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:16,777
and I know every pathetic
detail of your life,

78
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:19,940
Including your obvious
dual monster strategies.

79
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:21,350
I see.

80
00:05:21,433 --> 00:05:24,960
I had no idea that you were
such a big fan of mine.

81
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:28,057
So is that why you dragged
me all the way out here?

82
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:31,897
If you wanted my autograph, all
you had to do was ask me for it.

83
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:33,640
You make me sick, Kaiba.

84
00:05:33,860 --> 00:05:34,800
What did I do?

85
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:36,800
You ruined my life.

86
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:42,460
Now, this is all I have.

87
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:44,080
He's my family now.

88
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:47,757
You realize you're holding a
busted action figure, right?

89
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:51,520
You don't have any idea what
this thing means to me, Kaiba.

90
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:54,340
So you love your doll. How cute.

91
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:56,630
I do.

92
00:05:56,713 --> 00:05:58,500
Know why? Humor me.

93
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:00,780
It used to be my brothers!

94
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,880
But I'll never see him again.

95
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:07,611
Because your father took him away from me.

96
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:14,420
It was seven years ago today,
a day I'll never forget.

97
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:18,429
The tanks came back, but this
time it was worse than before.

98
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:21,060
The enemy wouldn't give up.

99
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:22,760
Not till they won.

100
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:25,680
Mikey, no!

101
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:31,601
You still have that thing, Mikey?

102
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:32,970
Yep.

103
00:06:33,053 --> 00:06:34,280
I know it's just a toy,

104
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:38,940
but soon the real Dynodude is going to
show up and beat up all the bad guys.

105
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:39,990
No kidding.

106
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:44,057
Well, then what's taking him so long
to get here and save the day already?

107
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:44,970
Don't worry.

108
00:06:45,220 --> 00:06:46,780
He's gonna be here soon.

109
00:06:47,020 --> 00:06:48,240
At least I hope.

110
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:49,990
Come on.

111
00:06:50,073 --> 00:06:51,537
It's not safe in here anymore.

112
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:52,450
Let's go.

113
00:06:53,740 --> 00:06:55,600
But we can't leave now.

114
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:57,830
Trust me.

115
00:06:58,580 --> 00:07:00,340
Are you sure about this?

116
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:01,900
Would Dynadude hide?

117
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:07,850
Where's Mom?

118
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:10,100
She's gone.

119
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:11,980
I know, where'd she go?

120
00:07:12,260 --> 00:07:13,400
She was captured.

121
00:07:14,260 --> 00:07:17,480
Oh, but I promise that
won't happen to you.

122
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,860
And soon we'll find Mom. Huh?

123
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,520
But until then, no!

124
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:24,180
It's the tanks!

125
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:25,820
Quick, follow me!

126
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:28,010
Help!

127
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:31,460
Mikey, where are you, pal?

128
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:34,820
They took him, they got my brother!

129
00:07:37,220 --> 00:07:42,520
Mikey, soon the real Dynatude will show
up Don't worry, he's gonna be here soon

130
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:48,600
No, Mikey, come back

131
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:56,146
Soon after he was taken, I found
out who was really responsible

132
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:58,877
We couldn't have done
this without you, Mr.

133
00:07:58,960 --> 00:07:59,790
Kaiba

134
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:05,260
I would have done
anything to get Mikey back

135
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,760
I can help you,

136
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:14,220
Alistair I know who took your
family away from you, my child

137
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:19,380
And if you do as I say, you'll
soon be reunited with them

138
00:08:20,420 --> 00:08:21,340
I will?

139
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:22,900
Who are you?

140
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:29,137
I'm a friend A friend who wants to see
justice served by helping you destroy

141
00:08:29,220 --> 00:08:33,749
the man who created the very tanks your
enemies used to capture your brother.

142
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:35,680
Tell me, who is it?

143
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:37,240
Gozaburo Kaiba.

144
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:40,320
Your father did this to me.

145
00:08:40,660 --> 00:08:44,740
Now you run his evil empire,
so it's your fault too.

146
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,780
That's not true.

147
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:55,460
It's time to pay for your father's crime
by giving up your soul to feed the beast.

148
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:56,700
That's not fair.

149
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:59,360
My brother's innocent!

150
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:00,810
Mokuba!

151
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:03,060
Our stepfather was a big jerk!

152
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:05,100
But don't blame Seto for that!

153
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:07,640
He knew that Gozabora was wrong!

154
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,297
That's why Seto took
control of Kaiba Corp and

155
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:12,968
changed it into a company
that helps people!

156
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:14,260
Sorry, Alistair!

157
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:17,160
But what happened to you is not our fault!

158
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:19,760
What do you know? A lot!

159
00:09:19,980 --> 00:09:24,333
You may not know this, but my brother
and I grew up without a family also!

160
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:25,677
You poor thing!

161
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:30,466
Now imagine what your life would be like
if you didn't have your brother either.

162
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:32,300
No, I can't.

163
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:34,227
Don't listen to him, Mokuba.

164
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:35,940
I'm just trying to help.

165
00:09:36,620 --> 00:09:37,680
How cute.

166
00:09:37,940 --> 00:09:39,240
A family spat.

167
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:40,940
Don't worry, Mokuba.

168
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:45,319
Your brother won't push you around
anymore once I take away his soul.

169
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:50,680
Take a look at yourself.

170
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:54,197
Everything you own was
paid for by Kaiba Corp.

171
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:55,497
The clothes you wear?

172
00:09:55,580 --> 00:09:56,840
The food you eat?

173
00:09:57,160 --> 00:09:59,720
That same money took my brother away.

174
00:10:00,060 --> 00:10:02,320
Well, it's time to pay me back.

175
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,920
By giving me your soul!

176
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:06,770
Wait a sec.

177
00:10:06,853 --> 00:10:09,000
You have a good point. I agree.

178
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:13,077
My stepfather was a snake, and what
he did to your family was wrong.

179
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:16,480
And you deserve to be
paid for that. Then again,

180
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:19,097
I don't really care for the way you got me

181
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:21,397
here by threatening to
put me out of business.

182
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:23,640
So why don't we continue this duel?

183
00:10:23,780 --> 00:10:27,297
And if you're lucky enough to win,
maybe I'll decide to help you out.

184
00:10:27,380 --> 00:10:30,880
When I defeat you in this
duel, you will help me.

185
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:32,440
Just you wait.

186
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:34,860
I activate Royal Decree.

187
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:40,320
As long as this card's in play, all other
trap cards on the field are useless.

188
00:10:40,860 --> 00:10:43,160
But I need my crush card to win.

189
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:48,000
I hope my little trap card didn't
put a damper on your strategy, Kaiba.

190
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:49,680
I end my turn.

191
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:51,880
That's what I thought.

192
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:56,060
All right, Gorlag, attack his
dragon with Firestorm Slash.

193
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:02,300
Now try a taste of your own monster.

194
00:11:02,780 --> 00:11:06,015
Versago the Destroyer, attack
his life points directly.

195
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:14,340
You're down to your last 400 points.

196
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:19,220
Thanks to my Gorlag's ability, the
monster you just lost belongs to me.

197
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:21,940
Only now, he's strong!

198
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:26,558
I have to summon a pretty
strong monster to stop him,

199
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:28,597
but I have nothing to sacrifice!

200
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:32,720
There's only one card that can
help, but I need to draw it now!

201
00:11:37,620 --> 00:11:40,857
I think I'll start this
round off by activating

202
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:44,317
a simple magic card
known as Card of Demise!

203
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:46,597
This lets me draw three cards!

204
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:48,040
Watch closely.

205
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:50,478
Here's where things get complicated.

206
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:53,660
Next, I'll activate White Dragon Ritual.

207
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:57,137
It lets me play one of my favorite cards,

208
00:11:57,220 --> 00:12:00,240
as long as I sacrifice a
powerful monster first.

209
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:05,520
So I'll send my mighty Blue-Eyes White
Dragon straight to the graveyard,

210
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:09,340
allowing me to summon
Paladin of White Dragon.

211
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:16,360
And now, I'll use Monster Reborn to
bring back my Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

212
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:23,420
Paladin, attack with Ionic Spear Burst!

213
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:32,820
And now that one of your fire monsters is
gone, your Gorlag loses 500 attack points.

214
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:38,960
Blue-Eyes White Dragon,
destroy his Gorlag!

215
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:51,100
I'm not ready for the fun to end just yet,
so I've got one more surprise for you.

216
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:53,717
Now I'll finish things
off by trading in my

217
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:56,329
paladin for another
blue-eyes white dragon.

218
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:03,860
If you thought I devastated
you this turn, then just wait.

219
00:13:04,120 --> 00:13:05,520
The worst is ahead.

220
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:06,910
Whatever.

221
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:12,240
I've got one word for
your moves. Predictable.

222
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:16,160
I can see your lame strategy
coming from a mile away.

223
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:20,068
If that's the case, then let's
see you do something about it.

224
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:22,020
I'll play a magic card.

225
00:13:22,420 --> 00:13:23,980
My pot of green.

226
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:26,060
It lets me draw two cards.

227
00:13:26,520 --> 00:13:30,600
Then I activate another magic
card called a Tonic's Flame.

228
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:37,697
How could you have destroyed
both of my dragons?

229
00:13:37,780 --> 00:13:40,940
You need to brush up on
your dual monsters' cards.

230
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:45,857
A tonic's flame destroys every creature
on the field that isn't a fire monster.

231
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:47,297
And as an added bonus,

232
00:13:47,380 --> 00:13:51,262
it allows me to bring my gorelag
back to the field in attack mode.

233
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:02,060
Next, I'll activate a magic
card known as Fire Whip.

234
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:08,260
My cards!

235
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:14,460
Thanks to my fire whip, your
precious blue eyes belong to me.

236
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:17,680
And they've been resurrected
as creatures of fire.

237
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:20,020
Those dragons are mine!

238
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:24,889
Call me crazy, but last I checked, your
dragons were on my side of the field.

239
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:28,616
Soon I'll use your favorite
monsters to take you down.

240
00:14:29,060 --> 00:14:31,080
Can you save perfect revenge?

241
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:40,120
Since my newly acquired
dragons are also fire monsters,

242
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:42,760
my Gorlag gets a 1,000-point boost.

243
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:47,957
You're staring into the
face of three unstoppable

244
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:51,160
creatures with a grand
total of 10,000 points.

245
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:53,540
But lucky for you, I can't attack.

246
00:14:53,780 --> 00:14:57,077
So I'll place one card
face down and end my turn.

247
00:14:57,160 --> 00:15:02,020
And thanks to the sacred seal of
Orichalcos, when you lose your life points,

248
00:15:02,220 --> 00:15:03,380
you lose your soul.

249
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:08,772
You'll suffer just like I did
at the hands of your father.

250
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:14,560
I'm down to my last 400 life
points and I'm out of moves.

251
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:17,800
There's not a card in my
deck that can save me now.

252
00:15:20,660 --> 00:15:21,820
What's going on?

253
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,100
I must be hallucinating

254
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:36,080
Kaiba, you have been chosen
to release the mighty Critias

255
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:39,640
All you have to do is remove the sword

256
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:55,920
All right.

257
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:58,957
I'm just about ready to
wake up from this dream.

258
00:15:59,040 --> 00:16:00,540
Now join forces.

259
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:02,720
Anything to shut you up.

260
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:09,580
Hey, look!

261
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:14,180
Well, what are you waiting for, Kaiba?

262
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:16,774
Are you going to play your card or not?

263
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:26,540
What's wrong with me?

264
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:28,240
I'm seeing things again.

265
00:16:29,100 --> 00:16:31,300
I never put this card in my deck.

266
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:35,337
And the picture looks exactly like
the dragon I just dreamt about.

267
00:16:35,420 --> 00:16:38,600
Is this another one of
Alistair's tricks? No.

268
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:40,140
Play this card.

269
00:16:40,320 --> 00:16:41,379
It's the only way.

270
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:45,680
Now, I play Fang of Critias. What?

271
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:47,320
You don't have that card.

272
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:48,814
What do you call this?

273
00:16:49,660 --> 00:16:54,100
Next, I'll merge my dragon with my
crush card to create a new monster!

274
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:56,340
No way!

275
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:59,326
But you can't fuse a
trap card with a monster!

276
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:02,820
Looks to me like I just did, Alistair.

277
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,420
Rise up, Doom Virus Dragon!

278
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:11,900
Big deal!

279
00:17:12,100 --> 00:17:13,159
Mine are stronger!

280
00:17:13,580 --> 00:17:14,410
True,

281
00:17:14,493 --> 00:17:17,677
but Doom Virus Dragon has a special
ability that automatically destroys

282
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:21,642
every monster on the field whose
attack strength is 1,500 or more.

283
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:27,960
So all your monsters are gone.

284
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:32,040
Now, Doom Virus Dragon, attack
his life points directly.

285
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:38,080
Game over. I win.

286
00:17:38,420 --> 00:17:40,420
You didn't beat me yet, Kaiba.

287
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:43,660
I activate Contagion of Madness.

288
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:51,100
Here's how it works.

289
00:17:51,420 --> 00:17:55,760
I lose 1,900 life points thanks
to your virus dragon's attack,

290
00:17:56,020 --> 00:17:59,740
but you lose 950 thanks to my magic card.

291
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:06,860
It's a draw.

292
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:11,690
Seto!

293
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:13,820
He's gone.

294
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:15,557
This isn't over.

295
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:19,400
I'll be back, and you'll pay
for what your father did to me!

296
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:29,120
Are we there yet?

297
00:18:33,220 --> 00:18:35,880
Hey, why'd we stop, man? Hey, wait!

298
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:38,162
Where do you think you're going?

299
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:41,050
That's weird.

300
00:18:41,133 --> 00:18:43,509
Why'd we stop at some
run-down gas station?

301
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:45,444
I don't like the looks of this.
